    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A great eastern state of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, founded on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a> peninsula by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiang-ziya">Jiang Ziya</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou</a> conquest.</li><li>Duke Huan and his minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guan-zhong">Guan Zhong</a> made Qi the first hegemon of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou</a> states in the 7th century BCE.</li><li>Its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/linzi">Linzi</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jixia-academy">Jixia Academy</a> made Qi a centre of wealth and philosophy until it surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> in 221 BCE.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Qi's later ruling family, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian">Tian</a>, descended from a prince of the State of Chen who had fled to Qi as a refugee in 672 BCE.</p></aside>
    </section>

